": \"For coordinate-defined planar geometries, Shapely provides deterministic area, length, distance, and topological predicates. It explicitly performs analysis in the x-y plane and ignores z.\",\n      \"read_scope\": \"Read the coordinate-system and geometry notes, measurement methods, and topological-predicate sections; not the full manual.\",\n      \"can_support\": \"After plan lines, room polygons, openings, and a scale-aware coordinate system have been traced, calculate 2D lengths/areas/distances and candidate contains/intersects/touches relations reproducibly.\",\n      \"cannot_support\": \"It does not extract or semantically recognize a drawing, establish that traced coordinates match a real building, or calculate roof slope from z; z is ignored in its geometric analysis.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Navigation-Oriented Topological Model Construction Algorithm for Complex Indoor Space\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.mdpi.com/2220-9964/12/6/248\",\n      \"locator\": \"Sections 3.2 (space-wall and room-room topology), 4.3 (polygon extraction), 4.5 (complexity), 5.1-5.3 (tests), and conclusion.\",\n      \"claim\": \"The paper constructs room polygons and adjacency/connectivity/inclusion relations from building-plan linework using graph and disjoint-set methods, and reports tests on real and simulated plans. Its conclusion says semantic extraction from plan annotations is outside the method's current treatment.\",\n      \"read_scope\": \"Read indexed full-text excerpts for the specified methods, tests, and conclusion. The publisher page was throttled, so this was not a full-paper read.\",\n      \"can_support\": \"A plan-derived topology baseline for room boundaries, wall incidence, adjacency, and connectivity, once linework is available.\",\n      \"cannot_support\": \"Automatic interpretation of untraced drawings, reliable semantic/material classification without annotation, or transfer of the reported algorithm's validity to Jingning dwellings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Neo4j Cypher Manual (current)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://neo4j.com/docs/cypher-manual/current/patterns/\",\n      \"locator\": \"Patterns and path matching: https://neo4j.com/docs/cypher-manual/current/patterns/ ; aggregating functions: https://neo4j.com/docs/cypher-manual/25/functions/aggregating/ ; spatial values and functions: https://neo4j.com/docs/cypher-manual/current/values-and-types/spatial/ and https://neo4j.com/docs/cypher-manual/current/functions/spatial/ .\",\n      \"claim\": \"Cypher MATCH expresses graph-pattern and path queries; count/avg/sum aggregate matched values; built-in spatial geometry is POINT (2D or 3D), with point distance requiring compatible CRS and dimensions. Spatial functions specify points and calculate point-to-point distance.\",\n      \"read_scope\": \"Read current pattern, spatial-value, and spatial-function pages; the official aggregation page was reviewed via its indexed excerpt for grouping and aggregate functions, not fully opened.\",\n      \"can_support\": \"Run graph rules, fixed/variable-length path queries, relationship integrity checks, and grouped counts/statistics; store coordinates/derived quantities and compute supported point-to-point distances.\",\n      \"cannot_support\": \"Without custom functions or a separate geometry engine, Cypher is not a drawing interpreter or general wall/polygon/solid geometry engine; graph paths alone do not calculate polygon area, shared-boundary length, or roof slope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"KICGPT: Large Language Model with Knowledge in Context for Knowledge Graph Completion\",\n      \"url\": \"https://aclanthology.org/2023.findings-emnlp.580/\",\n      \"locator\": \"Sections 1 and 3.1-3.3 define link prediction and candidate ranking; sections 4.1-4.2 describe benchmark data and MRR/Hits metrics; conclusion and limitations.\",\n      \"claim\": \"The paper treats completion as predicting and ranking a missing entity in an incomplete triple, combining a KG retriever with LLM re-ranking and demonstrations. It evaluates against held-out benchmark triples; this is predictive evaluation, not evidence verification for a particular building.\",\n      \"read_scope\": \"Read the abstract, problem definition, method, benchmark setup, metrics/results, and limitations; not a broader KGC survey.\",\n      \"can_support\": \"Use an LLM to propose/rank missing relation or label candidates, and evaluate predictions against deliberately hidden known triples in a controlled graph.\",\n      \"cannot_support\": \"A predicted material or construction relation is not verified merely because it is plausible, well-ranked, or supported by an LLM explanation; the paper does not validate claims against architectural drawings, field measurements, or Jingning evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Photogrammetry-based approach for collecting and processing information about an existing building\",\n      \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.24425/bpasts.2023.144453\",\n      \"locator\": \"Methods §§2.1-2.3; results and discussion §§3-4; conclusions §5.\",\n      \"claim\": \"In its single-building study, the UAV photogrammetry model represented geometry visible from outside and could not represent elements or structures not externally visible. Interior elements required a separate BIM model informed by plans and direct measurements. The study also recommends reference checks because individual take-offs could have material error even when an aggregate result looked accurate.\",\n      \"read_scope\": \"Read the abstract, UAV/model methods, model-comparison and take-off results, discussion, and conclusions.\",\n      \"can_support\": \"An explicit visibility boundary for external UAV oblique imagery and a rationale for independent reference dimensions and separate indoor capture.\",\n      \"cannot_support\": \"Internal room geometry, hidden joints/structure, material composition, or historical attributes from external imagery alone; its one-building accuracy figures are not guaranteed for another survey.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"methodOptions\": {\n    \"deterministic_geometry_baseline\": \"先固定坐标系、单位与图纸比例；比例未知时先用已知尺寸校准，并保留坐标及来源。两点长度 L=sqrt((dx)^2+(dy)^2)；高差 Δz=z2-z1；坡角 θ=atan2(|Δz|,sqrt((dx)^2+(dy)^2))×180/π，坡度比=|Δz|/水平投影。房间用平面多边形，墙线/柱点/门窗开口作为线或点；用相交、包含关系及正长度共享边界（阈值 ε）生成候选邻接/界面。由坐标公式或几何库计算，再把公式、单位、输入坐标、图纸页码和精度状态写回图谱。\",\n    \"neo4j_and_llm_boundary\": \"Neo4j负责对象与关系约束、路径查询、计数/分组统计；一般多段线和面几何由确定性几何步骤计算后写入图谱。LLM只提议缺失标签/关系候选；把候选、解释、模型与已提供来源分开保存，标记为预测或假设，证据不足时输出unknown/拒答，不自动升级为已证事实。\",\n    \"validation\": \"对预先设定的虚拟案例真值遮蔽一小部分尺寸/关系/材料标签，保留答案供盲测；长度/坡度与手算坐标基线对照并报绝对误差，关系/标签按precision、recall、F1核对，同时统计无依据断言、冲突和拒答。固定输入与随机种子，确保可复算。此结果只验证合成案例上的流程一致性与预测行为，不构成真实景宁民居的实证验证。\"\n  },\n  \"topologyRules\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WJ-01-v1\",\n      \"sourceIds\": [\n        \"S01\",\n        \"S03\"\n      ],\n      \"record\": \"构建方法与决策记录.md#r01用最少信息补齐墙与墙的交接\",\n      \"scope\": \"共同层位直线墙轴唯一交点\",\n      \"numericPolicy\": \"exact decimal fractions; no survey snapping\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WC-01-v1\",\n      \"sourceIds\": [\n        \"S03\"\n      ],\n      \"record\": \"构建方法与决策记录.md#r02墙柱推广与实施\",\n      \"scope\": \"轴对齐、端部平截、未扣洞墙矩形包络×统一地坪至最低墙顶；直立圆柱。内部重叠包含截面包含，不是OGC Overlaps专名。\",\n      \"numericPolicy\": \"exact decimal fractions; no survey tolerance\",\n      \"interpretation\": \"只有简化几何关系被确认；真实接触、嵌柱、裁切和受力均未确定\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"RS-01-v1\",\n      \"sourceIds\": [\n        \"S03\",\n        \"S07\"\n      ],\n      \"record\": \"构建方法与决策记录.md#r03坡面推广与实施\",\n      \"scope\": \"沿X拉伸、Z沿Y线性变化的凸四边形面，投影内部不重叠；三维共直线段；非通用曲面算法\",\n      \"numericPolicy\": \"exact decimal fractions for common boundary; floating point for derived area/slope\",\n      \"interpretation\": \"坡面无厚度、不继承屋顶木材/陶瓦标签；正脊是本例几何分类，不是独立构件或实地证据\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"topologySources\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"S01\",\n      \"title\": \"IFC 4.3.2.0 IfcConnectionTypeEnum\",\n      \"url\": \"https://standards.buildingsmart.org/IFC/RELEASE/IFC4_3/HTML/lexical/IfcConnectionTypeEnum.htm\",\n      \"locator\": \"6.1.2.7.1–.2\",\n      \"use\": \"连接部位词汇\",\n      \"checked\": \"2026-10-26\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"S03\",\n      \"title\": \"OGC 06-103r4 Simple feature access Part 1 v1.2.1\",\n      \"url\": \"https://docs.ogc.org/is/06-103r4/06-103r4.pdf\",\n      \"locator\": \"6.1.6.1; 6.1.10–6.1.13; 6.1.15.1–.3\",\n      \"use\": \"边界/内部/交集；多面片公共曲线，不提供本例墙柱或脊沟算法\",\n      \"checked\": \"2026-10-26\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"S07\",\n      \"title\": \"IFC4 FINAL IfcConnectionCurveGeometry\",\n      \"url\": \"https://standards.buildingsmart.org/IFC/RELEASE/IFC4/FINAL/HTML/schema/ifcgeometricconstraintresource/lexical/ifcconnectioncurvegeometry.htm\",\n      \"locator\": \"8.7.3.1 definition / attributes\",\n      \"use\": \"关联曲线几何的表达参考；本研究不声称完整IFC映射或物理连接成立\",\n      \"checked\": \"2026-10-26\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n",
